ians. Elizabeth and John Macarthur were the first married couple to travel voluntarily from Europe to Australia, arriving in 1790, both aged 23, within three years of the initial invasion. John Macarthur soon became famous in New South Wales and beyond as a wool pioneer, a politician, and a builder of farms at Parramatta and Camden. For a long time, Elizabeth’s life was regarded as contingent on John’s and, more recently, John’s on Elizabeth’s.","thumbnailUrl":"https://books.google.com/books/content?id=ipMjEQAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=1&source=gbs_api","experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Elizabeth Macarthur","confidence":0.98},{"name":"John Macarthur","confidence":0.98}],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Australia","confidence":0.95},{"name":"New South Wales","confidence":0.9}],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Elizabeth and John Macarthur’s lives are best understood as interdependent rather than one being merely contingent on the other.","confidence":0.62},"academicOrientation":{"score":35,"confidence":0.84},"profileConfidence":0.93,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Parramatta","confidence":0.72}]},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"c354c67cc27f795e1a97f7091910501992cd1a120d86a637d172dc97f5fa15ad","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"For a long time, Elizabeth’s life was regarded as contingent on John’s and, more recently, John’s on Elizabeth’s.","primarySubject":"History","primaryTopic":"Essays & Cultural Criticism","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"History","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"History","score":3,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"History","mappedSubject":"History","score":3,"confidence":"medium","sourceId":"source-google-books-elizabeth-and-john-the-macarthurs-of-elizabeth-farm-alan-atkinson","id":"subject-evidence-book-elizabeth-and-john